##Summary

Max-Heap Sort is a comparison-based sorting algorithm that uses a Max-Heap data structure to arrange elements in ascending order. In a Max-Heap, the value of every parent node is greater than or equal to the values of its child nodes.

The implementation begins by building a Max-Heap from the given array. After creating the heap, the largest element, which is present at the root, is exchanged with the last element of the array. The heap size is then reduced, and the heap property is restored using the heapify operation. This process is repeated until all elements are sorted.

##Conclusion

The implementation of the Max-Heap Sort algorithm demonstrates an efficient method of sorting elements using the Max-Heap data structure. By repeatedly moving the largest element to its correct position and restoring the heap property, the algorithm successfully sorts the given data.
